{
  "_what": "How each kind of notification looks: an icon name (Lucide, either casing), and a tone. Every notification's title and detail pass through the one failure-words gate (tools/ui/show/safe-error-card sanitize-error-text): a kind's `gate_words` are its words when the gate refuses, else `default_gate_words`; a detail that cannot pass is left out, and the raw words are the row's Details. Work still running without a measure draws the one loading animation (tools/ui/show/loading-mark); work with a measure fills a ring. The key is the kind a caller passes to notify(). A kind with no row here still draws with the fallback. Tones name screen-look notification tones in notifications.css. A notification draws as a glance row (tools/ui/show/listing-card), whose tones are the plain tone words; `listing_tones` turns a kind's tone, or a chip's badge tone, into one of them, and a chip whose tone turns into anything but the quiet tone is the row's state badge.",
  "words": {
    "together_unit": "like this",
    "together": "{count} notifications like this",
    "show_all": "Show all {count}",
    "show_fewer": "Show fewer",
    "read_all": "Mark all as read"
  },
